content.thinking:
Now I found the key info! From the docs:

1. `agents.defaults.model.fallbacks` - this is the main fallback chain. When the primary model fails, it falls back to the next model in this list.
2. From `faq-models.md`: "Model fallback to the next model in `agents.defaults.model.fallbacks`"
3. From `doctor.md`: `modelFallbacks` → `agents.defaults.model.primary/fallbacks`

So the way to auto-switch between DeepSeek models is:

```json
{
  "agents": {
    "defaults": {
      "model": {
        "primary": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro",
        "fallbacks": ["deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "deepseek/deepseek-chat"]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This means: if `deepseek-v4-pro` fails (rate limited, overloaded, etc.), OpenClaw will automatically fall back to `deepseek-v4-flash`, then `deepseek-chat`.

Let me present this to Robert clearly.

